{"shortDescription":"RNS Number : 6441T  Strategic Minerals PLC  07 September 2026   The information contained within this announcement is deemed by the Company to constitute inside information as stipulated under the Market Abuse Regulations (EU) No. 596/2014 ('MAR') which has been incorporated into UK law by the Euro…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":["RNS Number : 6441T  Strategic Minerals PLC  07 September 2026   ",{"type":"p","children":["The information contained within this announcement is deemed by the Company to constitute inside information as stipulated under the Market Abuse Regulations (EU) No. 596/2014 ('MAR') which has been incorporated into UK law by the European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018."]},{"type":"p","children":["7 September 2026"]},{"type":"p","children":["Strategic Minerals plc"]},{"type":"p","children":["(\"Strategic Minerals\" or the \"Company\")"]},{"type":"p","children":["Cobre Access Extended to 31 March 2031"]},{"type":"p","children":["Strategic Minerals (AIM: SML; USOTC: SMCDF), an international mineral exploration and production company, is pleased to announce that its wholly owned subsidiary, Southern Minerals Group LLC (\"SMG\"), has agreed an extension to its access to the Cobre magnetite stockpile in New Mexico, USA, to 31 March 2031."]},{"type":"p","children":["The extension provides SMG with continued access to the Cobre magnetite stockpile for a further two years beyond the current agreement, extending the term from 31 March 2029 to 31 March 2031 and supporting the Company's commitment to long-term site operations under the lease and continued capital investment in new mining equipment, as announced on 2 June 2026."]},{"type":"p","children":["The extension has been agreed through a Third Amendment to the existing Magnetite Sales Contract and all other terms of the existing agreement remain in full force and effect."]},{"type":"p","children":["Mark Burnett, Executive Director of Strategic Minerals, commented:"]},{"typ